  "description": {
    "text": "The JR East Pokémon Stamp Rally ran from 9 to 17 August 1997: participants had two days to visit 30 stations on Tokyo's Yamanote line and fill a stamp book with a different Pokémon stamp at each, and all 100,000 advance tickets sold out. Those who completed the book got a booklet holding matte reprints of two CoroCoro Comic promos, Mew and Surfing Pikachu."
